          "filename": "Georgetown Loop Railroad - 15 diesel locomotive (General Electric 47-ton engine) (22148591294).jpg",
          "caption": "This is a 47-ton, center-cab, narrow-gauge, switcher engine on display at the Colorado Railroad Museum in Golden, Colorado, USA.  It was built in 1943 by General Electric and used in Hawaii by the Railway and Land Company.  It was later put into service with the Camino, Cable &amp; Northern Railroad, a tourist railway in California.  After that, it was used by the Georgetown Loop Railroad in Colorado before being acquired by the Colorado Railroad Museum.\n\nThe \"GB&amp;L\" lettering seen on the cab in the above photo stands for the Georgetown, Breckenridge &amp; Leadville Railroad.",
